            "\n1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n   - The sensor measures the power radiated by the metal, denoted as $P$.\n   - The sensor displays the logarithm base 2 of the ratio of the power radiated to a reference power $P_0$.\n   - The reference power $P_0$ is a constant.\n   - The sensor is kept at a constant temperature of $487^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$.\n   - We need to find the value displayed by the sensor when the temperature of the metal surface is raised to $2767{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$.\n\n2. **Setting Up the Equation:**\n   - The sensor displays $\\log _{2}\\left(P / P_{0}\\right)$.\n   - When the temperature is $487^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the sensor shows a value of 1.\n   - Therefore, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\log _{2}\\left(P / P_{0}\\right) = 1\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solving for $P / P_0$:**\n   - Since $\\log _{2}\\left(P / P_{0}\\right) = 1$, we can rewrite this equation as:\n     \\[\n     P / P_{0} = 2^1\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying, we get:\n     \\[\n     P / P_{0} = 2\n     \\]\n\n4. **Finding the New Value:**\n   - When the temperature is raised to $2767{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the sensor displays a new value.\n   - Using the same equation, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\log _{2}\\left(P / P_{0}\\right) = \\log _{2}\\left(2\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Since $\\log _{2}\\left(2\\right) = 1$, the new value displayed by the sensor is:\n     \\[\n     \\log _{2}\\left(2\\right) = 1\n     \\]\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - The value displayed by the sensor when the temperature of the metal surface is raised to $2767{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is $\\boxed{1}$."
