            "To solve the problem, we start by simplifying the given equation:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\sec x + \\operatorname{cosec} x + 2(\\tan x - \\cot x) = 0\n\\]\n\nUsing the identities $\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}$ and $\\operatorname{cosec} x = \\frac{1}{\\sin x}$, we rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos x} + \\frac{1}{\\sin x} + 2(\\tan x - \\cot x) = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we express $\\tan x$ and $\\cot x$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$:\n\n\\[\n\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}, \\quad \\cot x = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos x} + \\frac{1}{\\sin x} + 2\\left(\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} - \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nCombining the terms, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos x} + \\frac{1}{\\sin x} + 2\\left(\\frac{\\sin^2 x - \\cos^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x}\\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cos x} + \\frac{1}{\\sin x} + 2\\left(\\frac{\\sin x - \\cos x}{\\sin x \\cos x}\\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nMultiplying through by $\\sin x \\cos x$ to clear the denominators, we obtain:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\sin x + \\cos x + 2(\\sin x - \\cos x) = 0\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3} \\sin x + \\cos x + 2 \\sin x - 2 \\cos x = 0\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we have:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 2) \\sin x - (1 + 2) \\cos x = 0\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n5 \\sin x - 3 \\cos x = 0\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by $\\cos x$, we obtain:\n\n\\[\n5 \\tan x - 3 = 0\n\\]\n\nSolving for $\\tan x$, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan x = \\frac{3}{5}\n\\]\n\nThe solutions for $x$ in the interval $(-\\pi, \\pi)$ are:\n\n\\[\nx = \\arctan \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = \\pi - \\arctan \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)\n\\]\n\nThe sum of these solutions is:\n\n\\[\n\\arctan \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right) + \\pi - \\arctan \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right) = \\pi\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of