          "question": "A farmer $F_{1}$ has a land in the shape of a triangle with vertices at $P(0,0), Q(1,1)$ and $R(2,0)$. From this land, a neighbouring farmer $F_{2}$ takes away the region which lies between the side $P Q$ and a curve of the form $y=x^{n}(n>1)$. If the area of the region taken away by the farmer $F_{2}$ is exactly $30 \\%$ of the area of $\\triangle P Q R$, then what is the value of $n$?",
          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Calculate the area of $\\triangle PQR$:**\n   \n   The vertices of $\\triangle PQR$ are $P(0,0)$, $Q(1,1)$, and $R(2,0)$. The area of a triangle can be calculated using the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n   \\]\n   Plugging in the coordinates:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(1 - 0) + 1(0 - 0) + 2(0 - 1) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -2 \\right| = 1\n   \\]\n   So, the area of $\\triangle PQR$ is $1$.\n\n2. **Determine the area taken away by $F_2$:**\n   \n   The area taken away by $F_2$ is $30\\%$ of the area of $\\triangle PQR$, which is:\n   \\[\n   0.30 \\times 1 = 0.3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Set up the equation for the area taken away by $F_2$:**\n   \n   The area taken away by $F_2$ is the area of the region between the line $PQ$ and the curve $y = x^n$. The line $PQ$ has a slope of $1$ and passes through the points $P(0,0)$ and $Q(1,1)$. The equation of the line $PQ$ is:\n   \\[\n   y = x\n   \\]\n   The area taken away by $F_2$ is the area of the region under the curve $y = x^n$ and above the line $y = x$. This area can be calculated using the formula for the area under a curve:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\int_{0}^{1} x^n \\, dx = \\left[ \\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} \\right]_{0}^{1} = \\frac{1^{n+1} - 0^{n+1}}{n+1} = \\frac{1}{n+1}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Set up the equation and solve for $n$:**\n   \n   We know that the area taken away by $F_2$ is $0.3$, so we set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{n+1} = 0.3\n   \\]\n   Solving for $n$:\n   \\[\n   n+1 = \\frac{1}{0.3} = \\frac{10}{3}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{10}{3} - 1 = \\frac{10}{3} - \\frac{3}{3} = \\frac{7}{3}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   \n   The value of $n$ is $\\frac{7}{3}$.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{n = \\frac{7}{3}}\n\\]",
