          "type": "Numeric",
          "question": "Galena (an ore) is partially oxidized by passing air through it at high temperature. After some time, the passage of air is stopped, but the heating is continued in a closed furnace such that the contents undergo self-reduction. What is the weight (in $\\mathrm{kg}$ ) of $\\mathrm{Pb}$ produced per $\\mathrm{kg}$ of $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ consumed?\n\n(Atomic weights in $\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}: \\mathrm{O}=16, \\mathrm{~S}=32, \\mathrm{~Pb}=207$ )",
          "model_outputs": [
            "To solve this problem, we need to determine the weight of lead produced per kilogram of oxygen consumed. We will use the given atomic weights of oxygen, sulfur, and lead to calculate the required values.\n\n1. **Calculate the weight of oxygen consumed:**\n   The weight of oxygen consumed is given by the mass of oxygen in the air that was used to oxidize the lead. The mass of oxygen in the air is calculated by multiplying the volume of air by the density of oxygen.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Mass of oxygen consumed} = \\frac{0.5 \\text{ kg}}{0.1 \\text{ L}} \\times 16 \\text{ g/L} = 8 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the mass of lead produced:**\n   The mass of lead produced is calculated by multiplying the mass of oxygen consumed by the atomic weight of lead.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Mass of lead produced} = 8 \\text{ kg} \\times 207 \\text{ g/mol} = 1656 \\text{ g}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the weight of lead produced per kilogram of oxygen consumed:**\n   To find the weight of lead produced per kilogram of oxygen consumed, we divide the mass of lead produced by the mass of oxygen consumed.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight of lead produced per kg of O}_2 = \\frac{1656 \\text{ g}}{8 \\text{ kg}} = 207 \\text{ g/kg}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Convert the weight of lead produced per kg of O}_2 to kilograms:**\n   To convert grams to kilograms, we divide by 1000.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Weight of lead produced per kg of O}_2 = \\frac{207 \\text{ g}}{1000} = 0.207 \\text{ kg/kg}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final answer:**\n   The weight of lead produced per kilogram of oxygen consumed is $\\boxed{0.207 \\text{ kg}}$.",
