            "\n1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n   We are given a set of complex numbers of the form \\(a + b \\omega + c \\omega^2\\) where \\(a, b, c\\) are distinct non-zero integers. We need to find the minimum value of the set \\(\\left\\{\\left|a+b \\omega+c \\omega^2\\right|^{2}: a, b, c \\text{ distinct non-zero integers}\\right\\}\\).\n\n2. **Properties of \\(\\omega\\):**\n   Since \\(\\omega\\) is a cube root of unity, it satisfies the equation \\(\\omega^3 = 1\\). This implies that \\(\\omega^2 + \\omega + 1 = 0\\).\n\n3. **Expression Simplification:**\n   We can simplify the expression \\(a + b \\omega + c \\omega^2\\) using the fact that \\(\\omega^2 + \\omega + 1 = 0\\):\n   \\[\n   a + b \\omega + c \\omega^2 = a + b \\omega + c (-\\omega - 1) = (a - c) + (b - c) \\omega\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the expression \\(a + b \\omega + c \\omega^2\\) can be rewritten as:\n   \\[\n   (a - c) + (b - c) \\omega\n   \\]\n\n4. **Magnitude Calculation:**\n   The magnitude of a complex number \\(z = x + yi\\) is given by \\(|z| = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}\\). Applying this to our expression:\n   \\[\n   \\left|a + b \\omega + c \\omega^2\\right| = \\sqrt{(a - c)^2 + (b - c)^2}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Minimizing the Magnitude:**\n   We need to minimize \\(\\sqrt{(a - c)^2 + (b - c)^2}\\). Since \\(a, b, c\\) are distinct non-zero integers, the minimum value of \\((a - c)^2 + (b - c)^2\\) occurs when \\(a, b, c\\) are consecutive integers.\n\n6. **Choosing Consecutive Integers:**\n   Let \\(a = n\\), \\(b = n+1\\), and \\(c = n+2\\) for some integer \\(n\\). Then:\n   \\[\n   (a - c)^2 + (b - c)^2 = (n - (n+2))^2 + ((n+1) - (n+2))^2 = 4\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the minimum value of \\(\\sqrt{(a - c)^2 + (b - c)^2}\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{4} = 2\n   \\]\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   The minimum value of the set \\(\\left\\{\\left|a+b \\omega+c \\omega^2\\right|^{2}: a, b, c \\text{ distinct non-zero integers}\\right\\}\\) is \\(2\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
