          "question": "Consider one mole of helium gas enclosed in a container at initial pressure $P_{1}$ and volume $V_{1}$. It expands isothermally to volume $4 V_{1}$. After this, the gas expands adiabatically and its volume becomes $32 V_{1}$. The work done by the gas during isothermal and adiabatic expansion processes are $W_{\\text {iso }}$ and $W_{\\text {adia }}$, respectively. If the ratio $\\frac{W_{\\text {iso }}}{W_{\\text {adia }}}=f \\ln 2$, then what is the value of $f$?",
          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Initial Setup**:\n   - We start with one mole of helium gas, which is enclosed in a container with initial pressure $P_1$ and volume $V_1$.\n   - The gas expands isothermally to a volume of $4V_1$.\n   - After this, the gas expands adiabatically to a volume of $32V_1$.\n\n2. **Work Done During Isothermal Expansion**:\n   - The work done by the gas during the isothermal expansion is given by the formula:\n     \\[\n     W_{\\text{iso}} = nRT \\ln\\left(\\frac{V_2}{V_1}\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Here, $n$ is the number of moles of gas, $R$ is the ideal gas constant, $T$ is the temperature, and $V_2$ is the final volume.\n   - Substituting the values, we get:\n     \\[\n     W_{\\text{iso}} = 1 \\times 0.0821 \\times 298 \\times \\ln\\left(\\frac{4V_1}{V_1}\\right) = 0.0821 \\times 298 \\times \\ln(4)\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying, we find:\n     \\[\n     W_{\\text{iso}} = 0.0821 \\times 298 \\times 1.386 \\approx 21.8 \\text{ J}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Work Done During Adiabatic Expansion**:\n   - The work done by the gas during the adiabatic expansion is given by the formula:\n     \\[\n     W_{\\text{adia}} = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{T} \\ln\\left(\\frac{V_2}{V_1}\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Here, $P_1$ is the initial pressure, $V_1$ is the initial volume, and $T$ is the final temperature.\n   - Substituting the values, we get:\n     \\[\n     W_{\\text{adia}} = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{T} \\ln\\left(\\frac{32V_1}{V_1}\\right) = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{T} \\ln(32)\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying, we find:\n     \\[\n     W_{\\text{adia}} = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{T} \\times 4.32 \\text{ J}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Ratio of Work Done**:\n   - The ratio of the work done during isothermal expansion to the work done during adiabatic expansion is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{W_{\\text{iso}}}{W_{\\text{adia}}} = \\frac{W_{\\text{iso}}}{W_{\\text{adia}}} = \\frac{21.8}{4.32} \\approx 5.1\n     \\]\n\n5. **Solving for $f$**:\n   - We are given that:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{W_{\\text{iso}}}{W_{\\text{adia}}} 