            "\n1. **Calculate the equivalent capacitance of the series combination**:\n   \n   The formula for the equivalent capacitance \\( C_{eq} \\) of two capacitors in series is:\n   \\[\n   C_{eq} = \\frac{C_1 \\cdot C_2}{C_1 + C_2}\n   \\]\n   \n   Substituting the given values:\n   \\[\n   C_{eq} = \\frac{2000 \\pm 10 \\mathrm{pF} \\cdot 3000 \\pm 15 \\mathrm{pF}}{2000 \\pm 10 \\mathrm{pF} + 3000 \\pm 15 \\mathrm{pF}}\n   \\]\n   \n   Since the error is small, we can approximate the values as:\n   \\[\n   C_{eq} \\approx \\frac{2000 \\cdot 3000}{2000 + 3000} = \\frac{6 \\times 10^6}{5 \\times 10^3} = 1200 \\mathrm{pF}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the energy stored in the series combination**:\n   \n   The formula for the energy \\( U \\) stored in a capacitor is:\n   \\[\n   U = \\frac{1}{2} C_{eq}^2 V^2\n   \\]\n   \n   Substituting the values:\n   \\[\n   U = \\frac{1}{2} (1200 \\mathrm{pF})^2 (5.00 \\pm 0.02 \\mathrm{V})^2\n   \\]\n   \n   Since the error is small, we can approximate the values as:\n   \\[\n   U \\approx \\frac{1}{2} (1200 \\cdot 5.00)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} (60000)^2 = 18000000 \\mathrm{J}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the error in the energy calculation**:\n   \n   The error in the energy calculation is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta U = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} C_{eq}^2 V^2\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{2} C_{eq}^2 V^2\\right)}\n   \\]\n   \n   Substituting the values:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta U = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} (1200 \\mathrm{pF})^2 (5.00 \\pm 0.02 \\mathrm{V})^2\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{2} (1200 \\mathrm{pF})^2 (5.00 \\pm 0.02 \\mathrm{V})^2\\right)}\n   \\]\n   \n   Since the error is small, we can approximate the values as:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta U \\approx \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} (60000)^2\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{2} (60000)^2\\right)} = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} (60000)^4\\right)} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2} (60000)^4} = \\frac{1}{2} (60000)^2 = 18000000 \\mathrm{J}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the percentage error**:\n   \n   The percentage error is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage Error} = \\left(\\frac{\\Delta U}{U}\\right) \\times 100\\%\n   \\]\n   \n   Substituting the values:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage Error} = \\left(\\frac{18000000 \\mathrm{J}}{18000000 \\mathrm{J}}\\right) \\times 100\\% = 100\\%\n   \\]\n\n5. **Conclusion**:\n   \n   The percentage error in the calculation of the energy stored in the series combination of capacitors is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{100\\%}\n   \\]",
