          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Calculate the change in volume of the block**:\n   The change in volume of the block can be calculated using the bulk modulus formula:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta V = -V \\frac{dP}{dV}\n   \\]\n   Given that the bulk modulus \\( K = 70 \\mathrm{GPa} \\) and the initial volume \\( V = 1 \\mathrm{m}^3 \\), we need to convert the bulk modulus to the same unit as the volume. Since \\( 1 \\mathrm{m}^3 = 1000 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3} \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   K = 70 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3 \\cdot \\text{Pa}^{-1}}\n   \\]\n   The change in volume \\( \\Delta V \\) is then:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta V = -70 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3 \\cdot \\text{Pa}^{-1}} \\times \\frac{1 \\mathrm{m}^3}{1000 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3}} = -70 \\times 10^3 \\times \\frac{1}{1000} = -70 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the change in edge length of the block**:\n   The change in edge length \\( \\Delta L \\) can be calculated using the formula for the edge length of a cubical solid:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta L = \\frac{\\Delta V}{V}\n   \\]\n   Given the initial edge length \\( L = 1 \\mathrm{m} = 1000 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}} \\) and the change in volume \\( \\Delta V = -70 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3} \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\Delta L = \\frac{-70 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3}}{1000 \\mathrm{ \\text{cm}^3}} = -0.07 \\mathrm{m}\n   \\]\n   Converting this to millimeters (since 1 meter = 1000 millimeters):\n   \\[\n   \\Delta L = -0.07 \\times 1000 = -70 \\mathrm{ \\text{mm}}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   The change in the edge length of the block is \\( -70 \\mathrm{ \\text{mm}} \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-70 \\text{ mm}}\n\\]",
