          "question": "An engineer is required to visit a factory for exactly four days during the first 15 days of every month and it is mandatory that no two visits take place on consecutive days. Then what is the number of all possible ways in which such visits to the factory can be made by the engineer during 1-15 June 2021?",
          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Understanding the Problem**:\n   - The engineer must visit the factory for exactly four days during the first 15 days of every month.\n   - No two visits can be on consecutive days.\n\n2. **Calculating the Total Number of Ways**:\n   - We need to find the number of ways to choose 4 days out of 15 such that no two chosen days are consecutive.\n   - This is a combinatorial problem where we need to select 4 days from 15, with the condition that no two selected days are adjacent.\n\n3. **Using Combinatorial Formula**:\n   - The number of ways to choose 4 days out of 15 such that no two chosen days are consecutive can be calculated using the formula for combinations with restrictions.\n   - The formula for combinations with restrictions is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\binom{n}{k} - \\binom{n-1}{k-1}\n     \\]\n     where \\( n \\) is the total number of items to choose from, and \\( k \\) is the number of items to choose.\n\n4. **Applying the Formula**:\n   - Here, \\( n = 15 \\) and \\( k = 4 \\).\n   - The formula becomes:\n     \\[\n     \\binom{15}{4} - \\binom{14}{3}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculating the Binomial Coefficients**:\n   - \\(\\binom{15}{4} = \\frac{15!}{4!(15-4)!} = \\frac{15 \\times 14 \\times 13 \\times 12}{4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 1365\\)\n   - \\(\\binom{14}{3} = \\frac{14!}{3!(14-3)!} = \\frac{14 \\times 13 \\times 12}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 364\\)\n\n6. **Subtracting the Results**:\n   - The number of ways to choose 4 days out of 15 such that no two chosen days are consecutive is:\n     \\[\n     1365 - 364 = 1001\n     \\]\n\n7. **Conclusion**:\n   - The number of all possible ways in which such visits to the factory can be made by the engineer during 1-15 June 2021 is \\( \\boxed{1001} \\).",
