e $\\vec{\\tau}$ at time $t$ is:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{\\tau} = \\vec{L} \\times \\vec{\\omega} = (20 \\mathrm{~kg} \\times \\mathrm{m}^{3} / \\mathrm{s}^{3}) \\times (10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}) = 200 \\mathrm{~kg} \\times \\mathrm{m}^{4} / \\mathrm{s}^{4}\n   \\]\n   \n   Therefore, the torque at time $t=2 \\mathrm{~s}$ is:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{\\tau} = 200 \\mathrm{~kg} \\times \\mathrm{m}^{4} / \\mathrm{s}^{4}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   Based on the calculations, the correct statement is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\text{C}}\n   \\]",
