}{3}}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculating $\\frac{625}{4} p_1$:**\n   Now, we need to find the value of $\\frac{625}{4} p_1$.\n   \n   \\[\n   \\frac{625}{4} p_1 = \\frac{625}{4} \\left( \\frac{\\binom{100}{3} - \\binom{80}{3}}{\\binom{100}{3}} \\right)\n   \\]\n   \n   Simplifying the expression, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{625}{4} p_1 = \\frac{625}{4} \\left( \\frac{\\binom{100}{3} - \\binom{80}{3}}{\\binom{100}{3}} \\right) = \\frac{625}{4} \\left( 1 - \\frac{\\binom{80}{3}}{\\binom{100}{3}} \\right)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n   The final answer is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\frac{625}{4} p_1}\n   \\]",
