            "\n1. **Calculate the determinant of matrix $E$:**\n   \\[\n   |E| = \\begin{vmatrix}\n   1 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n   2 & 3 & 4 \\\\\n   8 & 13 & 18\n   \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n   Expanding along the first row:\n   \\[\n   |E| = 1 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   3 & 4 \\\\\n   13 & 18\n   \\end{vmatrix} - 2 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   2 & 4 \\\\\n   8 & 18\n   \\end{vmatrix} + 3 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   2 & 3 \\\\\n   8 & 13\n   \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 18 - 4 \\cdot 13) - 2 \\cdot (2 \\cdot 18 - 4 \\cdot 8) + 3 \\cdot (2 \\cdot 13 - 3 \\cdot 8)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \\cdot (54 - 52) - 2 \\cdot (36 - 32) + 3 \\cdot (26 - 24)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot 4 + 3 \\cdot 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 2 - 8 + 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 0\n   \\]\n   Therefore, $|E| = 0$.\n\n2. **Calculate the determinant of matrix $P$:**\n   \\[\n   |P| = \\begin{vmatrix}\n   1 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n   0 & 0 & 1 \\\\\n   0 & 1 & 0\n   \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n   Expanding along the first row:\n   \\[\n   |P| = 1 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   0 & 1 \\\\\n   1 & 0\n   \\end{vmatrix} - 0 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   0 & 1 \\\\\n   0 & 0\n   \\end{vmatrix} + 0 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   0 & 0 \\\\\n   0 & 1\n   \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \\cdot (0 \\cdot 0 - 1 \\cdot 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \\cdot (-1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = -1\n   \\]\n   Therefore, $|P| = -1$.\n\n3. **Calculate the determinant of matrix $F$:**\n   \\[\n   |F| = \\begin{vmatrix}\n   1 & 3 & 2 \\\\\n   8 & 18 & 13 \\\\\n   2 & 4 & 3\n   \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n   Expanding along the first row:\n   \\[\n   |F| = 1 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   18 & 13 \\\\\n   4 & 3\n   \\end{vmatrix} - 3 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   8 & 13 \\\\\n   2 & 3\n   \\end{vmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}\n   8 & 18 \\\\\n   2 & 4\n   \\end{vmatrix}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \\cdot (18 \\cdot 3 - 13 \\cdot 4) - 3 \\cdot (8 \\cdot 3 - 13 \\cdot 2) + 2 \\cdot (8 \\cdot 4 - 18 \\cdot 2)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 1 \