          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Define the Arithmetic Progressions:**\n   - Let the first arithmetic progression have a common difference $d_1$ and the second arithmetic progression have a common difference $d_2$.\n   - Given that $d_1 d_2 = 10$, we can express $d_2$ in terms of $d_1$ as $d_2 = \\frac{10}{d_1}$.\n\n2. **Express the Lengths and Areas of the Rectangles:**\n   - The length of the $i$-th rectangle is $l_i = l_1 + (i-1)d_1$.\n   - The width of the $i$-th rectangle is $w_i = w_1 + (i-1)d_2$.\n   - The area of the $i$-th rectangle is $A_i = l_i \\cdot w_i = (l_1 + (i-1)d_1)(w_1 + (i-1)d_2)$.\n\n3. **Simplify the Area Expression:**\n   - Expand the area expression:\n     \\[\n     A_i = (l_1 + (i-1)d_1)(w_1 + (i-1)d_2)\n     \\]\n   - Using the fact that $d_2 = \\frac{10}{d_1}$, we can rewrite the expression as:\n     \\[\n     A_i = (l_1 + (i-1)d_1)\\left(w_1 + (i-1)\\left(\\frac{10}{d_1}\\right)\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Simplify further:\n     \\[\n     A_i = (l_1 + (i-1)d_1)\\left(w_1 + \\frac{10(i-1)}{d_1}\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Notice that $l_1$ and $w_1$ are constants, so we can factor out $l_1$ and $w_1$:\n     \\[\n     A_i = l_1 w_1 \\left(1 + \\frac{d_1}{10}\\right) \\left(1 + \\frac{i-1}{d_1}\\right)\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the Area Difference:**\n   - We are given that $A_{51} - A_{50} = 1000$.\n   - Using the expression for $A_i$, we can write:\n     \\[\n     A_{51} - A_{50} = l_1 w_1 \\left(1 + \\frac{d_1}{10}\\right) \\left(1 + \\frac{50}{d_1}\\right) - l_1 w_1 \\left(1 + \\frac{d_1}{10}\\right) \\left(1 + \\frac{50}{d_1}\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Notice that the terms involving $l_1 w_1$ cancel out:\n     \\[\n     A_{51} - A_{50} = l_1 w_1 \\left(1 + \\frac{d_1}{10}\\right) \\left(1 + \\frac{50}{d_1}\\right) - l_1 w_1 \\left(1 + \\frac{d_1}{10}\\right) \\left(1 + \\frac{50}{d_1}\\right) = 0\n     \\]\n   - This implies that $A_{51} = A_{50}$, which is consistent with the given condition.\n\n5. **Calculate the Area Difference for $A_{100} - A_{90}$:*