            "\n1. **Understanding the Reflection**:\n   The reflection of a point \\( Q \\) with respect to a plane can be represented by the formula:\n   \\[\n   S = 2 \\cdot \\frac{Q - \\vec{r}}{|\\vec{r}|}\n   \\]\n   where \\( \\vec{r} \\) is the position vector of the plane and \\( Q \\) is the position vector of the point \\( Q \\).\n\n2. **Given Information**:\n   - The position vector of \\( Q \\) is \\( 10 \\hat{i} + 15 \\hat{j} + 20 \\hat{k} \\).\n   - The position vector of \\( S \\) is \\( \\alpha \\hat{i} + \\beta \\hat{j} + \\gamma \\hat{k} \\).\n\n3. **Calculating the Reflection**:\n   - First, compute the vector \\( \\vec{r} \\):\n     \\[\n     \\vec{r} = -(t+p) \\hat{i} + t \\hat{j} + (1+p) \\hat{k}\n     \\]\n   - Next, compute the magnitude of \\( \\vec{r} \\):\n     \\[\n     |\\vec{r}| = \\sqrt{(-(t+p))^2 + t^2 + (1+p)^2}\n     \\]\n   - Then, compute the vector \\( \\frac{Q - \\vec{r}}{|\\vec{r}|} \\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{Q - \\vec{r}}{|\\vec{r}|} = \\frac{(10 \\hat{i} + 15 \\hat{j} + 20 \\hat{k}) - (-(t+p) \\hat{i} + t \\hat{j} + (1+p) \\hat{k})}{|\\vec{r}|}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = \\frac{(10 + t + p) \\hat{i} + (15 - t - 1 - p) \\hat{j} + (20 - 1 - p) \\hat{k}}{|\\vec{r}|}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Scaling the Reflection**:\n   - The reflection \\( S \\) is given by:\n     \\[\n     S = 2 \\cdot \\frac{Q - \\vec{r}}{|\\vec{r}|}\n     \\]\n   - Substituting the expression for \\( \\frac{Q - \\vec{r}}{|\\vec{r}|} \\):\n     \\[\n     S = 2 \\cdot \\frac{(10 + t + p) \\hat{i} + (15 - t - 1 - p) \\hat{j} + (20 - 1 - p) \\hat{k}}{|\\vec{r}|}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Comparing with Given Position Vector**:\n   - Given \\( S = \\alpha \\hat{i} + \\beta \\hat{j} + \\gamma \\hat{k} \\), we equate the coefficients:\n     \\[\n     2 \\cdot \\frac{(10 + t + p) \\hat{i} + (15 - t - 1 - p) \\hat{j} + (20 - 1 - p) \\hat{k}}{|\\vec{r}|} = \\alpha \\hat{i} + \\beta \\hat{j} + \\gamma \\hat{k}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Solving for Coefficients**:\n   - Equating the coefficients of \\( \\hat{i} \\), \\( \\hat{j} \\), and \\( \\hat{k} \\):\n     \\[\n     2 \\cdot \\frac{10 + t + p}{|\\vec{r}|} = \\alpha\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2 \\cdot \\frac{15 - t - 1 - p}{|\\vec{r}|} = \\beta\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2 \\cdot \\frac{20 - 1 - p}{|\\vec{r}|} = \\gamma\n     \\]\n\n7. **Calculating the Sum of Coefficients**:\n   - Summing the coefficients:\n     \\[\n     \\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 2 \\left( \\frac{10 + t + p}{|\\vec{r}|} + \\frac{15 - t - 1 - p}{|\\vec{r}|} + \\frac{20 - 1 - p}{|\\vec{r}|} \\right)\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying the expression:\n     \\[\n     \\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 2 \\left( \\frac{10 + 15 + 20}{|\\vec{r}|} + \\frac{t + p - t - 1 - p}{|\\vec{r}|} \\right)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 2 \\left( \\frac{45}{|\\vec{r}|} + \\frac{-1}{|\\vec{r}|} \\right)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     = 2 \\left( \\frac{44}{|\\vec{r}|} \\right)\n     \\]\n\n8. **Substituting the Magnitude**:\n   - Since \\( |\\vec{r}| = \\sqrt{(-(t+p))^2 + t^2 + (1+p)^2} \\):\n     \\[\n     \\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = 2 \\left( \\frac{44}{\\sqrt{(-(t+p))^2 + t^2 + (1+p)^2}} \\right)\n     \\]\n\n9. **Evaluating the Options**:\n   - The correct option is:\n     \\[\n     \\boxed{3(\\alpha+\\beta)=-101}\n     \\]\n\nConclusion:\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{3(\\alpha+\\beta)=-101}\\).",
