ft[ v^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\cdot v^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\right]_{1}^{\\log_2 9}\n\\]\n\nEvaluating the antiderivative at the bounds:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (9^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1^{\\frac{1}{3}}) - (1^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1^{\\frac{1}{3}}) \\right] = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (9^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1) - (1 - 1) \\right] = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (9^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1) \\right]\n\\]\n\n**Combining the results**\n\nNow, we combine the results from both parts:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\left[ (9 \\log_2 9 - 2 \\log_2 2) - 7 \\right] + \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (9^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1) \\right]\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\left[ (9 \\log_2 9 - 2 \\log_2 2) - 7 \\right] + \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (9^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1) \\right] = \\frac{1}{3} \\left[ (9 \\log_2 9 - 2 \\log_2 2) - 7 \\right] + \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (9^{\\frac{1}{3}} - 1) \\right]\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer**\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.5}\n\\]",
