          "type": "MCQ",
          "question": "Atom $\\mathrm{X}$ occupies the fcc lattice sites as well as alternate tetrahedral voids of the same lattice. The packing efficiency (in \\%) of the resultant solid is closest to\n\n(A) 25\n\n(B) 35\n\n(C) 55\n\n(D) 75",
          "model_outputs": [
            "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the packing efficiency of the solid formed by the fcc lattice sites and alternate tetrahedral voids.\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the fcc lattice sites:**\n   The volume of a face-centered cubic (fcc) lattice is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{fcc}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3\n   \\]\n   where \\(a\\) is the lattice constant.\n\n2. **Calculate the volume of the alternate tetrahedral voids:**\n   The volume of a tetrahedral void is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{tetra}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2}\n   \\]\n   where \\(a\\) is the lattice constant.\n\n3. **Calculate the total volume of the solid:**\n   The total volume of the solid is the sum of the volume of the fcc lattice sites and the volume of the alternate tetrahedral voids:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{total}} = V_{\\text{fcc}} + V_{\\text{tetra}}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the packing efficiency:**\n   The packing efficiency is the ratio of the total volume of the solid to the volume of the unit cell:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{V_{\\text{total}}}{V_{\\text{unit cell}}}\n   \\]\n   where \\(V_{\\text{unit cell}}\\) is the volume of the unit cell.\n\n5. **Substitute the values and calculate the packing efficiency:**\n   Let's assume the lattice constant \\(a = 2\\) for simplicity. Then:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{fcc}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{tetra}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{2} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{total}} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{\\pi + 2}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{unit cell}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{\\frac{\\pi + 2}{6}}{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} = \\frac{\\pi + 2}{\\pi}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the numerical value of the packing efficiency:**\n   Using \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14159\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{3.14159 + 2}{3.14159} = \\frac{5.14159}{3.14159} \\approx 1.64\n   \\]\n\n7. **Convert the packing efficiency to a percentage:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} \\approx 1.64 \\times 100\\% \\approx 166.4\\%\n   \\]\n\nThe closest packing efficiency to 166.4% is **55%**.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{55}\n\\]",
            "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the packing efficiency of the solid formed by the fcc lattice sites and alternate tetrahedral voids.\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the fcc lattice sites:**\n   The volume of a face-centered cubic (fcc) lattice is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{fcc}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3\n   \\]\n   where \\(a\\) is the lattice constant.\n\n2. **Calculate the volume of the alternate tetrahedral voids:**\n   The volume of a tetrahedral void is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{tetra}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2}\n   \\]\n   where \\(a\\) is the lattice constant.\n\n3. **Calculate the total volume of the solid:**\n   The total volume of the solid is the sum of the volume of the fcc lattice sites and the volume of the alternate tetrahedral voids:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{total}} = V_{\\text{fcc}} + V_{\\text{tetra}}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the packing efficiency:**\n   The packing efficiency is the ratio of the total volume of the solid to the volume of the unit cell:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{V_{\\text{total}}}{V_{\\text{unit cell}}}\n   \\]\n   where \\(V_{\\text{unit cell}}\\) is the volume of the unit cell.\n\n5. **Substitute the values and calculate the packing efficiency:**\n   Let's assume the lattice constant \\(a = 2\\) for simplicity. Then:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{fcc}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{tetra}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{2} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{total}} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{\\pi + 2}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{unit cell}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{\\frac{\\pi + 2}{6}}{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} = \\frac{\\pi + 2}{\\pi}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the numerical value of the packing efficiency:**\n   Using \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14159\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{3.14159 + 2}{3.14159} = \\frac{5.14159}{3.14159} \\approx 1.64\n   \\]\n\n7. **Convert the packing efficiency to a percentage:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} \\approx 1.64 \\times 100\\% \\approx 166.4\\%\n   \\]\n\nThe closest packing efficiency to 166.4% is **55%**.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{55}\n\\]",
            "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the packing efficiency of the solid formed by the fcc lattice sites and alternate tetrahedral voids.\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the fcc lattice sites:**\n   The volume of a face-centered cubic (fcc) lattice is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{fcc}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^3\n   \\]\n   where \\(a\\) is the lattice constant.\n\n2. **Calculate the volume of the alternate tetrahedral voids:**\n   The volume of a tetrahedral void is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{tetra}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2} \\times \\frac{a}{2}\n   \\]\n   where \\(a\\) is the lattice constant.\n\n3. **Calculate the total volume of the solid:**\n   The total volume of the solid is the sum of the volume of the fcc lattice sites and the volume of the alternate tetrahedral voids:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{total}} = V_{\\text{fcc}} + V_{\\text{tetra}}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the packing efficiency:**\n   The packing efficiency is the ratio of the total volume of the solid to the volume of the unit cell:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{V_{\\text{total}}}{V_{\\text{unit cell}}}\n   \\]\n   where \\(V_{\\text{unit cell}}\\) is the volume of the unit cell.\n\n5. **Substitute the values and calculate the packing efficiency:**\n   Let's assume the lattice constant \\(a = 2\\) for simplicity. Then:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{fcc}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{tetra}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{2} \\times \\frac{2}{2} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1 \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{total}} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{\\pi + 2}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{unit cell}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{6}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{\\frac{\\pi + 2}{6}}{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} = \\frac{\\pi + 2}{\\pi}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the numerical value of the packing efficiency:**\n   Using \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14159\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} = \\frac{3.14159 + 2}{3.14159} = \\frac{5.14159}{3.14159} \\approx 1.64\n   \\]\n\n7. **Convert the packing efficiency to a percentage:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Packing Efficiency} \\approx 1.64 \\times 100\\% \\approx 166.4\\%\n   \\]\n\nThe closest packing efficiency to 166.4% is **55%**.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{55}\n\\]"
