\n1. **Evaluate the integral of \\( f(x) \\) over the interval \\([0, 1]\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\int_0^1 f(x) \\, dx\n   \\]\n   We need to evaluate this integral using the given piecewise function:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\int_0^{\\frac{1}{2n}} n(1-2nx) \\, dx + \\int_{\\frac{1}{2n}}^{\\frac{3}{4n}} 2n(2nx-1) \\, dx + \\int_{\\frac{3}{4n}}^{\\frac{1}{n}} 4n(1-nx) \\, dx + \\int_{\\frac{1}{n}}^1 \\frac{n}{n-1}(nx-1) \\, dx\n   \\]\n\n2. **Evaluate each integral:**\n   Let's evaluate each integral step by step:\n   \\[\n   \\int_0^{\\frac{1}{2n}} n(1-2nx) \\, dx = \\left[ nx - n^2x^2 \\right]_0^{\\frac{1}{2n}} = n \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n} - n^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2n}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{n^2}{4n^2} = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int_{\\frac{1}{2n}}^{\\frac{3}{4n}} 2n(2nx-1) \\, dx = \\left[ 2n^2x^2 - 2nx \\right]_{\\frac{1}{2n}}^{\\frac{3}{4n}} = 2n^2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4n} - 2n \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n} - \\left(2n^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n} - 2n \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n}\\right) = \\frac{3}{2} - 1 - (1 - 1) = \\frac{3}{2} - 1 = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int_{\\frac{3}{4n}}^{\\frac{1}{n}} 4n(1-nx) \\, dx = \\left[ 4n - 4n^2x \\right]_{\\frac{3}{4n}}^{\\frac{1}{n}} = 4n - 4n^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{n} - \\left(4n - 4n^2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4n}\\right) = 4n - 4 - (4n - 3) = 4n - 4n + 3 = 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int_{\\frac{1}{n}}^1 \\frac{n}{n-1}(nx-1) \\, dx = \\left[ \\frac{n}{n-1}x^2 - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\right]_{\\frac{1}{n}}^1 = \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot 1^2 - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{n}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n} - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot 1\\right) = \\frac{n}{n-1} - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n^2} - \\left(\\frac{n}{n-1} - \\frac{n}{n-1}\\right) = \\frac{n}{n-1} - \\frac{1}{n^2} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{n^2} - \\frac{1}{n^2} = \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Combine the results:**\n   Now, we combine the results of the four integrals:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{4} 