            "\n1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n   We are given a function \\( f(x) \\) defined on the interval \\([0, 1]\\) with the following piecewise definition:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = \\begin{cases}\n   n(1-2nx) & \\text{if } 0 \\leq x \\leq \\frac{1}{2n} \\\\\n   2n(2nx-1) & \\text{if } \\frac{1}{2n} \\leq x \\leq \\frac{3}{4n} \\\\\n   4n(1-nx) & \\text{if } \\frac{3}{4n} \\leq x \\leq \\frac{1}{n} \\\\\n   \\frac{n}{n-1}(nx-1) & \\text{if } \\frac{1}{n} \\leq x \\leq 1\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n   We are also given that the area of the region bounded by the curves \\( x=0, x=1, y=0 \\) and \\( y=f(x) \\) is 4.\n\n2. **Calculating the Area:**\n   To find the area of the region bounded by the curves \\( x=0, x=1, y=0 \\) and \\( y=f(x) \\), we need to integrate the function \\( f(x) \\) over the interval \\([0, 1]\\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\int_0^1 f(x) \\, dx\n   \\]\n   We will evaluate this integral using the given piecewise function:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\int_0^{\\frac{1}{2n}} n(1-2nx) \\, dx + \\int_{\\frac{1}{2n}}^{\\frac{3}{4n}} 2n(2nx-1) \\, dx + \\int_{\\frac{3}{4n}}^{\\frac{1}{n}} 4n(1-nx) \\, dx + \\int_{\\frac{1}{n}}^1 \\frac{n}{n-1}(nx-1) \\, dx\n   \\]\n\n3. **Evaluating Each Integral:**\n   Let's evaluate each integral step by step:\n   \\[\n   \\int_0^{\\frac{1}{2n}} n(1-2nx) \\, dx = \\left[ nx - n^2x^2 \\right]_0^{\\frac{1}{2n}} = n \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n} - n^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2n}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{n^2}{4n^2} = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int_{\\frac{1}{2n}}^{\\frac{3}{4n}} 2n(2nx-1) \\, dx = \\left[ 2n^2x^2 - 2nx \\right]_{\\frac{1}{2n}}^{\\frac{3}{4n}} = 2n^2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4n} - 2n \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n} - \\left(2n^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n} - 2n \\cdot \\frac{1}{2n}\\right) = \\frac{3}{2} - 1 - (1 - 1) = \\frac{3}{2} - 1 = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int_{\\frac{3}{4n}}^{\\frac{1}{n}} 4n(1-nx) \\, dx = \\left[ 4n - 4n^2x \\right]_{\\frac{3}{4n}}^{\\frac{1}{n}} = 4n - 4n^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{n} - \\left(4n - 4n^2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4n}\\right) = 4n - 4 - (4n - 3) = 4n - 4n + 3 = 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int_{\\frac{1}{n}}^1 \\frac{n}{n-1}(nx-1) \\, dx = \\left[ \\frac{n}{n-1}x^2 - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\right]_{\\frac{1}{n}}^1 = \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot 1^2 - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{n}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n} - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot 1\\right) = \\frac{n}{n-1} - \\frac{n}{n-1} \\cdot \\frac{1}{n^2} - \\left(\\frac{n}{n-1} - \\frac{n}{n-1}\\right) = \\frac{n}{n-1} - \\frac{1}{n^2} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{n^2} - \\frac{1}{n^2} = \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combining the Results:**\n   Now, we combine the results of the four integrals:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 + \\frac{n^2 - n - 1}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{2} + 3 +