          "question": "A person of height $1.6 \\mathrm{~m}$ is walking away from a lamp post of height $4 \\mathrm{~m}$ along a straight path on the flat ground. The lamp post and the person are always perpendicular to the ground. If the speed of the person is $60 \\mathrm{~cm} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$, then what is the speed of the tip of the person's shadow on the ground with respect to the person in $\\mathrm{cm} \\mathrm{s}^{-1}$?",
          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Define the variables and given information:**\n   - Let $h$ be the height of the person above the ground.\n   - Let $v$ be the speed of the person in meters per second.\n   - Let $s$ be the height of the lamp post above the ground.\n   - Let $t$ be the time taken for the person to reach the lamp post.\n\n2. **Set up the equations based on the given information:**\n   - The person is walking away from the lamp post, so the distance covered by the person is $s - h$.\n   - The person's speed is given as $60 \\mathrm{~cm} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$, which is $0.6 \\mathrm{~m} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$.\n   - The time taken to reach the lamp post is $t = \\frac{s - h}{0.6}$.\n\n3. **Calculate the speed of the tip of the person's shadow:**\n   - The tip of the person's shadow is at a height of $h + s$.\n   - The speed of the tip of the person's shadow is given by the Pythagorean theorem:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Speed of the tip of the shadow} = \\sqrt{(h + s)^2 + h^2}\n     \\]\n   - Substitute $s = h + 4$ (since the lamp post is 4 meters above the ground):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Speed of the tip of the shadow} = \\sqrt{(h + (h + 4))^2 + h^2} = \\sqrt{(2h + 4)^2 + h^2}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n     \\[\n     (2h + 4)^2 + h^2 = 4h^2 + 16h + 16 + h^2 = 5h^2 + 16h + 16\n     \\]\n   - Substitute $h = 1.6$ into the expression:\n     \\[\n     5(1.6)^2 + 16(1.6) + 16 = 5 \\times 2.56 + 25.6 + 16 = 12.8 + 25.6 + 16 = 54.4\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, the speed of the tip of the person's shadow is:\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{54.4} = 7.35 \\mathrm{~cm} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The speed of the tip of the person's shadow on the ground with respect to the person is $\\boxed{7.35 \\mathrm{~cm} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}}$.",
