          "gold": "512",
          "index": 11,
          "type": "Integer",
          "question": "Let $A_{1}, A_{2}, A_{3}, \\ldots, A_{8}$ be the vertices of a regular octagon that lie on a circle of radius 2. Let $P$ be a point on the circle and let $P A_{i}$ denote the distance between the points $P$ and $A_{i}$ for $i=1,2, \\ldots, 8$. If $P$ varies over the circle, then what is the maximum value of the product $P A_{1} \\cdot P A_{2} \\cdots P A_{8}?",
          "model_outputs": [
            "\n1. **Understanding the Problem:**\n   - We have a regular octagon with vertices $A_1, A_2, A_3, \\ldots, A_8$ on a circle with radius 2.\n   - Let $P$ be a point on the circle.\n   - We need to find the maximum value of the product $P A_1 \\cdot P A_2 \\cdots P A_8$.\n\n2. **Geometric Interpretation:**\n   - Consider the product $P A_1 \\cdot P A_2 \\cdots P A_8$.\n   - This product can be interpreted as the product of the distances from point $P$ to each vertex of the octagon.\n\n3. **Using the Power of a Point:**\n   - The power of a point $P$ with respect to a circle is defined as $PA_1 \\cdot PA_2 \\cdots PA_8$.\n   - The power of a point $P$ with respect to a circle is also equal to $OP^2 - r^2$, where $O$ is the center of the circle and $r$ is the radius of the circle.\n\n4. **Maximizing the Power:**\n   - Since $P$ is on the circle, the power of $P$ is maximized when $P$ is at the point on the circle that is farthest from the center of the circle.\n   - The maximum power occurs when $P$ is at the point on the circle that is diametrically opposite to the center of the circle.\n\n5. **Calculating the Maximum Power:**\n   - The radius of the circle is 2, so the distance from the center of the circle to any vertex of the octagon is 2.\n   - The maximum power occurs when $P$ is at the point on the circle that is diametrically opposite to the center of the circle.\n   - The distance from the center of the circle to this point is $2 + 2 = 4$.\n   - Therefore, the maximum power is $4^2 - 2^2 = 16 - 4 = 12$.\n\n6. **Conclusion:**\n   - The maximum value of the product $P A_1 \\cdot P A_2 \\cdots P A_8$ is $\\boxed{12}$.",
